kitty: smooth cursor motion, ported from alacritty-smooth-cursor

Port of the smooth cursor animation from
https://github.com/GregTheMadMonk/alacritty-smooth-cursor (patch/smooth-cursor
branch, commit 6d1c2604) to kitty. Made against kitty v0.49.2.

The cursor is drawn as a rectangle whose edges ease exponentially towards the
real cursor, leading edges faster than trailing ones, so it stretches while it
moves. While animating, the real cursor is hidden and the rectangle is drawn
over the finished frame, sampling it to keep the text below readable.

New options (all off/default unless set in kitty.conf or with -o):

    cursor_smooth_motion              no      enable the animation
    cursor_smooth_motion_factor       0.2     fraction of the distance covered per 1/60 s
    cursor_smooth_motion_spring       0.8     factor multiplier for the trailing edges
    cursor_smooth_motion_max_stretch  3 2     max width/height while moving, in cursor sizes
    cursor_smooth_motion_antijitter   50      min ms between changes of the target

Apply with:  git apply kitty-smooth-cursor.patch   (or: patch -p1 < kitty-smooth-cursor.patch)
If kitty/options/{parse.py,types.py,to-c-generated.h} conflict after an update,
apply the rest with --exclude for those three files and regenerate them with
./kitty/launcher/kitty +launch gen/config.py after building once.

